WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.810
- I'm the one who reacts.

00:00:05.598 --> 00:00:07.581
- [Walt Jr.] What the hell is this?

00:00:07.581 --> 00:00:08.414
- [Skyler] Hey.

00:00:08.414 --> 00:00:10.368
- [Walter] It's veggie
bacon. We're watching

00:00:10.368 --> 00:00:12.118
our cholesterol, I guess.

00:00:12.118 --> 00:00:14.515
- [Walt Jr.] Not me, I want real bacon.

00:00:14.515 --> 00:00:16.858
- (laughing) This feels
like my struggle right now

00:00:16.858 --> 00:00:18.308
cause I'm watching my cholesterol.

00:00:18.308 --> 00:00:20.988
It's more about decreasing
the amount of saturated fat

00:00:20.988 --> 00:00:24.388
in your diet, decreasing
fatty foods, fried foods,

00:00:24.388 --> 00:00:28.521
and also at the same time,
increasing your insoluble fiber.

00:00:28.521 --> 00:00:31.354
(Walter coughing)

00:00:39.098 --> 00:00:40.998
Oh no, don't faint, don't faint.

00:00:40.998 --> 00:00:41.868
If you're ever feeling lightheaded,

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:43.708
the first thing you should
do is get down on the floor.

00:00:43.708 --> 00:00:45.978
The biggest danger of
passing out is actually

00:00:45.978 --> 00:00:48.198
hitting your head and causing
a subdural hemorrhage.

00:00:48.198 --> 00:00:50.288
So please, if you're feeling woozy,

00:00:50.288 --> 00:00:52.623
get down, get support, call for help.

00:00:52.623 --> 00:00:55.423
- [Walter] This is so
embarrassing, I am fine, honestly.

00:00:56.599 --> 00:00:59.128
It's just some bug going
around. First my wife had it,

00:00:59.128 --> 00:01:04.128
then my son and now me,
it's just like a chest cold.

00:01:04.438 --> 00:01:07.188
- See, it's important to
not minimize your symptoms.

00:01:07.188 --> 00:01:08.808
Is it possible that he has a chest cold?

00:01:08.808 --> 00:01:11.718
Sure, but why in the world
did he pass out from standing?

00:01:11.718 --> 00:01:13.778
That needs to be further investigated

00:01:13.778 --> 00:01:15.908
and it needs to be
investigated by an ER team

00:01:15.908 --> 00:01:18.088
cause he could be having a
heart attack for all they know.

00:01:18.088 --> 00:01:19.631
- [Paramedic] Lean
forward for me, would you?

00:01:23.188 --> 00:01:25.138
Mr. White, are you a smoker?

00:01:25.138 --> 00:01:26.651
- [Walter] No, never.

00:01:29.418 --> 00:01:30.261
Why do you ask?

00:01:32.121 --> 00:01:34.478
- Okay, this is where these shows,

00:01:34.478 --> 00:01:35.798
things get a little ridiculous.

00:01:35.798 --> 00:01:38.598
The paramedic with the power
of a stethoscope can diagnose

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:39.918
if there's some really serious

00:01:39.918 --> 00:01:41.718
issue going on like lung cancer.

00:01:41.718 --> 00:01:43.618
At most, you can hear lung sounds

00:01:43.618 --> 00:01:45.598
that can happen as a
result of a pneumonia,

00:01:45.598 --> 00:01:48.348
of a viral infection,
an inflammatory process,

00:01:48.348 --> 00:01:51.778
a tumor, but you can't
know that without scanning.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:54.758
So this like devious,
mischievous, look of him going

00:01:54.758 --> 00:01:59.287
ah by listening with the
stethoscope is pure ridiculous.

00:01:59.287 --> 00:02:01.537
(rumbling)

00:02:10.584 --> 00:02:12.751
(ringing)

00:02:19.016 --> 00:02:22.878
- [Doctor] Mr. White? Mr. White?

00:02:24.348 --> 00:02:25.181
- Yes.

00:02:26.818 --> 00:02:29.748
- You understood what
I've just said to you.

00:02:29.748 --> 00:02:31.178
- Yes.

00:02:31.178 --> 00:02:33.488
Lung cancer. Inoperable.

00:02:33.488 --> 00:02:35.008
- I'm really glad they're
showing this part.

00:02:35.008 --> 00:02:36.478
When you're receiving bad news,

00:02:36.478 --> 00:02:38.258
it's really difficult to comprehend.

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:39.768
You just got a diagnosis that you're

00:02:39.768 --> 00:02:41.478
potentially sick for
the rest of your life.

00:02:41.478 --> 00:02:43.638
Or going to lose your life
earlier than you expected.

00:02:43.638 --> 00:02:44.478
You're not going to be like, okay,

00:02:44.478 --> 00:02:46.128
so what are the next
steps of what I should do?

00:02:46.128 --> 00:02:47.888
So whenever you deliver
bad news as a doctor,

00:02:47.888 --> 00:02:49.558
you have to have the patient come back.

00:02:49.558 --> 00:02:51.348
You have to have someone with the patient

00:02:51.348 --> 00:02:53.138
to help them understand what's going on.

00:02:53.138 --> 00:02:55.168
This part could be the most accurate

00:02:55.168 --> 00:02:57.048
part of the first season.

00:02:57.048 --> 00:02:59.088
- [Walter] Lung cancer. Inoperable.

00:02:59.088 --> 00:03:00.398
- I also don't know how they realize

00:03:00.398 --> 00:03:03.418
that it's an inoperable so
quickly, a little bit out there.

00:03:03.418 --> 00:03:04.938
I don't know how much
time has passed here.

00:03:04.938 --> 00:03:06.748
It's a little inaccurate.

00:03:06.748 --> 00:03:11.748
- [Walter] It's just, you've
got mustard on your...

00:03:11.798 --> 00:03:14.068
- This is almost like a
dissociation process where

00:03:14.068 --> 00:03:17.228
to escape from the bad
news, he's reverting back

00:03:17.228 --> 00:03:19.948
to like a childhood state,
or a less serious state

00:03:19.948 --> 00:03:21.118
and thinking about the mustard.

00:03:21.118 --> 00:03:23.028
Cause that's more fixable
in the given moment.

00:03:23.028 --> 00:03:24.348
This does happen. Maybe this is

00:03:24.348 --> 00:03:26.408
a little bit more exaggerated though.

00:03:26.408 --> 00:03:29.077
- Heisenberg says relax.

00:03:29.077 --> 00:03:32.718
(sighs) I'm relaxed. I'm relaxed.

00:03:32.718 --> 00:03:33.726
I'm relaxed--

00:03:33.726 --> 00:03:35.241
- Oh!

00:03:35.241 --> 00:03:37.824
(men grunting)

00:03:42.675 --> 00:03:44.614
(exclaiming)

00:03:44.614 --> 00:03:45.828
- Wow, damn man, look at that. Look.

00:03:45.828 --> 00:03:48.478
- I'm not surprised if
he broke a few knuckles,

00:03:48.478 --> 00:03:51.858
hitting a skull on the floor
like that over and over again.

00:03:51.858 --> 00:03:53.028
Remember when you punched someone

00:03:53.028 --> 00:03:54.698
standing up, their head moves back.

00:03:54.698 --> 00:03:56.578
So there's no excess force placed

00:03:56.578 --> 00:03:57.668
on your knuckle on your bone.

00:03:57.668 --> 00:03:59.318
But when they're laying down
and you're hitting them,

00:03:59.318 --> 00:04:01.168
you're essentially hitting the concrete

00:04:01.168 --> 00:04:04.451
with your bare knuckle,
you're breaking stuff.

00:04:06.007 --> 00:04:09.818
- Heisenberg! What's the matter with you?

00:04:09.818 --> 00:04:11.168
- It looks like he's having a seizure.

00:04:11.168 --> 00:04:13.221
Sometimes that can
happen with brain bleeds.

00:04:13.221 --> 00:04:16.098
- [Walter] There's, there's no pulse.

00:04:16.098 --> 00:04:17.238
- If there's no pulse you've gotta start

00:04:17.238 --> 00:04:19.831
chest compressions, chest
compressions, chest compressions.

00:04:19.831 --> 00:04:21.238
- Do something.

00:04:21.238 --> 00:04:22.071
- [Walter] Do something?

00:04:22.071 --> 00:04:24.488
He needs an ambulance.
He needs a hospital.

00:04:24.488 --> 00:04:28.601
- Do something! You're
smart, right? Do that thing!

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.128
- He knows that thing!

00:04:30.128 --> 00:04:32.038
But the thing is really
meant to buy your time.

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:33.868
It doesn't actually restart the heart.

00:04:33.868 --> 00:04:36.038
The point of doing the thing
so that the ambulance has time

00:04:36.038 --> 00:04:38.358
to get there and actually intervene.

00:04:38.358 --> 00:04:39.191
- Beans.

00:04:40.678 --> 00:04:42.041
- Castor beans.

00:04:43.648 --> 00:04:45.391
- So what are we gonna do with them?

00:04:45.391 --> 00:04:47.108
- We are going to process them into ricin.

00:04:47.108 --> 00:04:49.588
- You actually process it into castor oil

00:04:49.588 --> 00:04:52.078
and the residue has ricin in it.

00:04:52.078 --> 00:04:53.061
- Rice and beans.

00:04:55.768 --> 00:04:56.601
- Ricin.

00:04:57.487 --> 00:04:59.658
- He said rice and beans.
I forgot about this.

00:04:59.658 --> 00:05:01.948
- It's an extremely effective poison.

00:05:01.948 --> 00:05:03.658
It's toxic in small doses.

00:05:03.658 --> 00:05:06.388
Also fairly easy to
overlook during an autopsy.

00:05:06.388 --> 00:05:08.368
- It is checked for on
autopsy's by the way,

00:05:15.646 --> 00:05:17.745
This his fugue state?

00:05:17.745 --> 00:05:19.308
- What's the last thing you remember?

00:05:20.755 --> 00:05:23.578
- Well, I was driving home.

00:05:25.175 --> 00:05:26.185
I think.

00:05:26.185 --> 00:05:28.085
- From what I remember, he's faking this

00:05:28.085 --> 00:05:29.635
and he's doing a really good job.

00:05:29.635 --> 00:05:31.995
- Isn't it possible
that this had something

00:05:31.995 --> 00:05:34.085
to do with all the
prescriptions I've been taking.

00:05:34.085 --> 00:05:37.735
- In order to diagnose a
medication side effect like that

00:05:37.735 --> 00:05:39.855
it really has to be a
diagnosis of exclusion

00:05:39.855 --> 00:05:41.655
where you rule everything else out

00:05:41.655 --> 00:05:44.505
that could cause this
dissociative state of his,

00:05:44.505 --> 00:05:46.785
and then you can then
blame the medication,

00:05:46.785 --> 00:05:49.445
but you absolutely do need
a psychiatric consult here.

00:05:49.445 --> 00:05:52.425
- Would you tell me about
patient confidentiality?

00:05:52.425 --> 00:05:54.925
- It's very straightforward.
Without your permission

00:05:54.925 --> 00:05:57.325
I can't disclose anything
you tell me to anyone.

00:05:57.325 --> 00:05:58.805
- What about my family?

00:05:58.805 --> 00:06:02.079
- Not to your family, not to
the police, not to anyone.

00:06:02.079 --> 00:06:03.615
The only exception would be if

00:06:03.615 --> 00:06:05.295
you threatened to kill someone,

00:06:05.295 --> 00:06:08.185
then I'd be able to tell that
person. But only that person.

00:06:08.185 --> 00:06:09.495
- Protected health information is

00:06:09.495 --> 00:06:11.285
really important in the cases of

00:06:11.285 --> 00:06:13.425
homicidal or suicidal ideation.

00:06:13.425 --> 00:06:16.495
We do alert the authorities or loved ones.

00:06:16.495 --> 00:06:18.605
I don't know that in
a homicidal situation,

00:06:18.605 --> 00:06:20.115
if you threaten to harm one other person,

00:06:20.115 --> 00:06:21.285
they only tell that person.

00:06:21.285 --> 00:06:24.485
I think they have to notify
the authorities as well.

00:06:24.485 --> 00:06:26.728
- Jesse, wake up.

00:06:28.463 --> 00:06:29.713
Jesse, wake up.

00:06:32.805 --> 00:06:36.295
- That is a needle and a syringe

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:38.978
likely to have been used for narcotics.

00:06:44.224 --> 00:06:46.391
(choking)

00:06:47.585 --> 00:06:49.845
Oh no. If someone's
throwing up on their back,

00:06:49.845 --> 00:06:51.415
you have to put them on their side

00:06:51.415 --> 00:06:52.955
in order to help clear their airway.

00:06:52.955 --> 00:06:54.085
Because if they can't protect their

00:06:54.085 --> 00:06:55.325
airway cause they're unconscious,

00:06:55.325 --> 00:06:58.441
they can aspirate the vomit, choke, die.

00:06:58.441 --> 00:06:59.702
(choking)

00:06:59.702 --> 00:07:01.333
- No, no, no.

00:07:01.333 --> 00:07:03.500
(choking)

00:07:06.085 --> 00:07:07.498
- Dude. You got to act.

00:07:14.885 --> 00:07:18.065
And that's unfortunately how
a lot of overdoses do end.

00:07:18.065 --> 00:07:20.465
Someone ends up aspirating
and choking to death.

00:07:25.466 --> 00:07:27.799
(gun shots)

00:07:29.435 --> 00:07:31.152
Oh, that's got to hurt.

00:07:31.152 --> 00:07:32.631
- Oh, that's gotta hurt.

00:07:32.631 --> 00:07:34.615
(breaking glass)

00:07:34.615 --> 00:07:36.595
- That's one way to crush your femur,

00:07:36.595 --> 00:07:38.525
create a fatty embolism, make it go to

00:07:38.525 --> 00:07:41.069
your lungs and you just die instantly.

00:07:41.069 --> 00:07:43.902
(tires squealing)

00:07:45.335 --> 00:07:46.775
Also don't forget, crush injuries

00:07:46.775 --> 00:07:49.135
release a massive amount
of electrolytes into the

00:07:49.135 --> 00:07:50.785
bloodstream from the damaged cells

00:07:50.785 --> 00:07:52.985
and create a complete mashup of your

00:07:52.985 --> 00:07:54.535
electrical system in the body,

00:07:54.535 --> 00:07:56.805
which most importantly
happens in the heart.

00:07:56.805 --> 00:07:58.556
Therefore it could be lethal.

00:07:58.556 --> 00:08:01.139
(horn honking)

00:08:03.175 --> 00:08:06.295
How come like bad guys in
movies always walk so calmly.

00:08:06.295 --> 00:08:07.888
Like they're never in a rush.

00:08:09.795 --> 00:08:11.635
Like my guy, you don't
think the cops are coming

00:08:11.635 --> 00:08:13.909
after you just lit up a parking lot?

00:08:13.909 --> 00:08:16.935
(horn beeping)

00:08:16.935 --> 00:08:21.008
- No, muy fácil.

00:08:25.585 --> 00:08:27.385
- Yeah. The bad guy's not in a rush.

00:08:29.485 --> 00:08:31.765
He lit up a supermarket.
He's not in a rush.

00:08:31.765 --> 00:08:32.778
He's getting his ax.

00:08:33.775 --> 00:08:36.178
An ax to the head is
incompatible with life.

00:08:37.325 --> 00:08:39.492
(gunshot)

00:08:40.345 --> 00:08:42.555
GSW to the head, incompatible with life.

00:08:42.555 --> 00:08:45.335
Thought I'd, thought
I'd let you guys know.

00:08:45.335 --> 00:08:46.778
- No, impossible.

00:08:56.265 --> 00:08:57.098
Salud.

00:09:00.621 --> 00:09:03.954
(both speaking Spanish)

00:09:07.125 --> 00:09:09.792
(water running)

00:09:16.889 --> 00:09:19.309
(man gagging)

00:09:19.309 --> 00:09:21.165
- Induction of vomiting
for poison can work.

00:09:21.165 --> 00:09:23.065
It has to happen very rapidly.

00:09:23.065 --> 00:09:24.655
Remember ricin gets absorbed

00:09:24.655 --> 00:09:27.935
very quickly into your mucus membranes.

00:09:27.935 --> 00:09:30.665
That's why it can affect
you even through your eyes.

00:09:30.665 --> 00:09:33.045
Can you make it less
lethal if you vomit it up?

00:09:33.045 --> 00:09:33.928
Yeah, probably.

00:09:35.534 --> 00:09:38.117
(upbeat music)

00:09:40.047 --> 00:09:42.959
(glass breaking)

00:09:42.959 --> 00:09:43.792
- Tu!

00:09:49.014 --> 00:09:50.398
- I feel like if this was true ricin

00:09:50.398 --> 00:09:52.268
there would be a lot of vomiting here.

00:09:55.933 --> 00:10:00.350
Those are Pyxis machines.
Those look very legitimate.

00:10:02.566 --> 00:10:03.399
- Visto.

00:10:05.638 --> 00:10:08.099
- It's like a full
operating room in there.

00:10:08.099 --> 00:10:09.035
- Vamanos.

00:10:09.035 --> 00:10:11.795
- Those hospital beds are
so extremely expensive.

00:10:11.795 --> 00:10:13.348
You have no idea.

00:10:15.249 --> 00:10:16.832
- Rapiddo, rapiddo!

00:10:17.775 --> 00:10:18.865
- I mean you have to intubate him.

00:10:18.865 --> 00:10:20.445
You have to make sure
his heart's not stopped.

00:10:20.445 --> 00:10:22.105
These are the most crucial moments

00:10:22.105 --> 00:10:23.955
in order to help save someone's life.

00:10:26.075 --> 00:10:29.495
Oh, I have no idea what he
just squirted into his mouth.

00:10:29.495 --> 00:10:31.735
- (exclaiming)

00:10:31.735 --> 00:10:33.505
- All right. And she's
bagging way too fast.

00:10:33.505 --> 00:10:35.085
When you're bagging, you need to bag

00:10:35.085 --> 00:10:36.995
at the same rate that
a person would breathe.

00:10:36.995 --> 00:10:39.335
If we're at rest, you're bagging
at pow, pow, pow, pow, pow,

00:10:39.335 --> 00:10:41.398
you could actually
create a bigger problem.

00:10:42.635 --> 00:10:44.735
They're doing an intubation it looks like.

00:10:46.745 --> 00:10:48.445
Some leads that aren't sticking well,

00:10:48.445 --> 00:10:50.228
starting IVs, all good stuff.

00:10:53.835 --> 00:10:58.428
They're doing dialysis to
get rid of the poison. Wow.

00:11:02.025 --> 00:11:03.995
That's a blood transfusion,

00:11:03.995 --> 00:11:06.618
O negative blood, universal donor.

00:11:08.875 --> 00:11:09.708
Oh!

00:11:11.965 --> 00:11:13.415
- Gracias.

00:11:13.415 --> 00:11:15.965
- I love that he's chilling
already. Not realistic.

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:24.057
(bell rings)

00:11:29.553 --> 00:11:31.048
- (exclaims)

00:11:31.048 --> 00:11:33.602
- (explosion) Oh!

00:11:33.602 --> 00:11:35.091
Kaboom.

00:11:35.091 --> 00:11:35.924
- (alarm ringing)

00:11:35.924 --> 00:11:37.358
- Kaboom. Not surviving that.

00:11:39.416 --> 00:11:40.374
- (alarm ringing)

00:11:40.374 --> 00:11:41.388
- Oh, maybe I was wrong.

00:11:43.275 --> 00:11:45.105
I love how the staff are in no concern

00:11:45.105 --> 00:11:47.704
that there is another explosion
that's about to happen.

00:11:47.704 --> 00:11:49.375
- (alarm ringing)

00:11:49.375 --> 00:11:52.395
- Oh, okay. Yeah. He's not fixing his tie.

00:11:52.395 --> 00:11:55.305
That's ridiculous. This isn't Batman.

00:11:55.305 --> 00:11:56.965
Did you know that I'm a YouTube boxer now?

